{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011xcqSrkeUqzeDaZiGwvujp","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"LearnLM Eedi randomized controlled trial UK secondary schools tutoring remediation arxiv\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Testing the efficacy of AI tutoring in secondary mathematics: A scaled RCT in UK classrooms\",\"url\":\"https://www.socialscienceregistry.org/trials/18079\"},{\"title\":\"AI Tutoring: UK RCT Outcomes\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/papers/2512.23633\"},{\"title\":\"AI Tutors, With a Little Human Help, Offer ‘Reliable’ Instruction, Study Finds\",\"url\":\"https://www.the74million.org/article/ai-tutors-with-a-little-human-help-offer-reliable-instruction-study-finds/\"},{\"title\":\"Eedi Showing How AI Tutoring Can Deliver Personalized Learning Safely And Effectively - Learning Engineering Virtual Institute\",\"url\":\"https://learning-engineering-virtual-institute.org/eedi-showing-how-ai-tutoring-can-deliver-personalized-learning-safely-and-effectively/\"},{\"title\":\"[2512.23633] AI tutoring can safely and effectively support students: An exploratory RCT in UK classrooms\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.23633\"},{\"title\":\"AI tutoring can safely and effectively support students: An exploratory RCT in UK classrooms\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2512.23633\"},{\"title\":\"AI Tutoring Can Safely And Effectively Support Students: An Exploratory RCT In UK Classrooms - Learning Engineering Virtual Institute\",\"url\":\"https://learning-engineering-virtual-institute.org/ai-tutoring-can-safely-and-effectively-support-students-an-exploratory-rct-in-uk-classrooms/\"},{\"title\":\"goo.gle/LearnLM-Nov25 2025-11-11 AI tutoring can safely and effectively support\",\"url\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/deepmind-media/LearnLM/learnLM_nov25.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Whole School SEND (WSS) Review: study protocol for a two-arm pragmatic parallel cluster randomised controlled trial in 160 English secondary schools\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC8107406/\"}]\n\nI found relevant research on the LearnLM and Eedi randomized controlled trial. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Study Overview\n\nAn exploratory randomized controlled trial was conducted with 165 students across five UK secondary schools to evaluate AI tutoring effectiveness. LearnLM—a generative AI model fine-tuned for pedagogy—was integrated into chat-based tutoring sessions on the Eedi mathematics platform, with expert tutors directly supervising LearnLM and revising each message it drafted until they would be satisfied sending it themselves.\n\n## Study Design\n\nThe trial recruited 165 students in Years 9 and 10 (ages 13–15) across five schools and ran from May through June 2025. Students were randomly assigned to receive either static pedagogical support (pre-written hints) or interactive one-to-one tutoring sessions, with tutoring students further randomized to receive either an expert human tutor or LearnLM supervised by a human tutor.\n\n## Key Findings\n\nLearnLM proved to be a reliable source of pedagogical instruction, with supervising tutors approving 76.4% of its drafted messages making zero or minimal edits. The exploratory RCT provided initial evidence that AI tutoring can support student mathematics learning at levels similar to expert human tutoring.\n\n## Future Research\n\nA scaled trial aims to recruit and randomize 1,200 students across UK secondary schools over a full school term, with students in AI tutoring arms receiving interactive tutoring with different levels of contextual information.\n\nThe paper is available on arXiv as arxiv:2512.23633.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8c941fff-a85c-417c-ae34-d68a383e6ff3","uuid":"5585d83d-7ca8-4d49-b704-b56859b073fb","timestamp":"2026-08-11T00:22:26.395Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"LearnLM Eedi randomized controlled trial UK secondary schools tutoring remediation arxiv","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_0155CbX7zv16DFWtccWo25DS","content":[{"title":"Testing the efficacy of AI tutoring in secondary mathematics: A scaled RCT in UK classrooms","url":"https://www.socialscienceregistry.org/trials/18079"},{"title":"AI Tutoring: UK RCT Outcomes","url":"https://www.emergentmind.com/papers/2512.23633"},{"title":"AI Tutors, With a Little Human Help, Offer ‘Reliable’ Instruction, Study Finds","url":"https://www.the74million.org/article/ai-tutors-with-a-little-human-help-offer-reliable-instruction-study-finds/"},{"title":"Eedi Showing How AI Tutoring Can Deliver Personalized Learning Safely And Effectively - Learning Engineering Virtual Institute","url":"https://learning-engineering-virtual-institute.org/eedi-showing-how-ai-tutoring-can-deliver-personalized-learning-safely-and-effectively/"},{"title":"[2512.23633] AI tutoring can safely and effectively support students: An exploratory RCT in UK classrooms","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.23633"},{"title":"AI tutoring can safely and effectively support students: An exploratory RCT in UK classrooms","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2512.23633"},{"title":"AI Tutoring Can Safely And Effectively Support Students: An Exploratory RCT In UK Classrooms - Learning Engineering Virtual Institute","url":"https://learning-engineering-virtual-institute.org/ai-tutoring-can-safely-and-effectively-support-students-an-exploratory-rct-in-uk-classrooms/"},{"title":"goo.gle/LearnLM-Nov25 2025-11-11 AI tutoring can safely and effectively support","url":"https://storage.googleapis.com/deepmind-media/LearnLM/learnLM_nov25.pdf"},{"title":"Whole School SEND (WSS) Review: study protocol for a two-arm pragmatic parallel cluster randomised controlled trial in 160 English secondary schools","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC8107406/"}]},"I found relevant research on the LearnLM and Eedi randomized controlled trial. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Study Overview\n\nAn exploratory randomized controlled trial was conducted with 165 students across five UK secondary schools to evaluate AI tutoring effectiveness. LearnLM—a generative AI model fine-tuned for pedagogy—was integrated into chat-based tutoring sessions on the Eedi mathematics platform, with expert tutors directly supervising LearnLM and revising each message it drafted until they would be satisfied sending it themselves.\n\n## Study Design\n\nThe trial recruited 165 students in Years 9 and 10 (ages 13–15) across five schools and ran from May through June 2025. Students were randomly assigned to receive either static pedagogical support (pre-written hints) or interactive one-to-one tutoring sessions, with tutoring students further randomized to receive either an expert human tutor or LearnLM supervised by a human tutor.\n\n## Key Findings\n\nLearnLM proved to be a reliable source of pedagogical instruction, with supervising tutors approving 76.4% of its drafted messages making zero or minimal edits. The exploratory RCT provided initial evidence that AI tutoring can support student mathematics learning at levels similar to expert human tutoring.\n\n## Future Research\n\nA scaled trial aims to recruit and randomize 1,200 students across UK secondary schools over a full school term, with students in AI tutoring arms receiving interactive tutoring with different levels of contextual information.\n\nThe paper is available on arXiv as arxiv:2512.23633."],"durationSeconds":8.762300457999983,"searchCount":1}}
