{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BzAJHXMXxgxVxjx88TU8hy","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Bastani Sungu \"Generative AI\" \"harm learning\" PNAS 2025 high school mathematics citation volume\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Correction for Bastani et al., Generative AI without guardrails can harm learning: Evidence from high school mathematics | PNAS\",\"url\":\"https://www.pnas.org/doi/10.1073/pnas.2518204122\"},{\"title\":\"Generative AI Without Guardrails Can Harm Learning: Evidence from High School Mathematics by Hamsa Bastani, Osbert Bastani, Alp Sungu, Haosen Ge, Özge Kabakcı, Rei Mariman :: SSRN\",\"url\":\"https://papers.ssrn.com/sol3/papers.cfm?abstract_id=4895486\"},{\"title\":\"Generative AI without guardrails can harm learning: Evidence from high school mathematics - PubMed\",\"url\":\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/40560616/\"},{\"title\":\"Correction for Bastani et al., Generative AI without guardrails can harm learning: Evidence from high school mathematics - PMC\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12403119/\"},{\"title\":\"Generative AI without guardrails can harm learning: Evidence from high school mathematics | PNAS\",\"url\":\"https://www.pnas.org/doi/10.1073/pnas.2422633122\"},{\"title\":\"Generative AI without guardrails can harm learning: Evidence from high school mathematics - Center for Health Incentives and Behavioral Economics (CHIBE)\",\"url\":\"https://chibe.upenn.edu/publications/generative-ai-without-guardrails-can-harm-learning-evidence-from-high-school-mathematics/\"},{\"title\":\"Generative AI without guardrails can harm learning: Evidence from high school mathematics\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/393011815_Generative_AI_without_guardrails_can_harm_learning_Evidence_from_high_school_mathematics\"},{\"title\":\"The Effortless Trap: Productive Struggle, AI, and the Illusion of Learning\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2606.26181\"},{\"title\":\"A Meta-Analysis of LLM Effects on Students across Qualification, Socialisation, and Subjectification\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2509.22725\"},{\"title\":\"Transforming GenAI Policy to Prompting Instruction: An RCT of Scalable Prompting Interventions in a CS1 Course\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2602.16033\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found the paper you're looking for:\n\nThe article \"Generative AI Without Guardrails Can Harm Learning: Evidence from High School Mathematics\" by Hamsa Bastani, Osbert Bastani, Alp Sungu, Haosen Ge, Özge Kabakcı, and Rei Mariman was published in the Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences (PNAS), volume 122, issue 26, in 2025.\n\nThe study involved a field experiment where nearly a thousand high school math students were provided with access to generative AI tutors. Two different generative AI tutors were deployed: one mimicking a standard ChatGPT interface (\"GPT Base\") and one with prompts designed to safeguard learning (\"GPT Tutor\").\n\n**Citation information:**\n- DOI: 10.1073/pnas.2422633122\n- Volume 122, Issue 26, published July 2025\n\nThe paper has been cited in several recent academic works and continues to be relevant to discussions about generative AI's impact on student learning.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8c941fff-a85c-417c-ae34-d68a383e6ff3","uuid":"781ec135-7371-4506-8eba-2ecb40f67a5e","timestamp":"2026-08-11T00:25:05.686Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Bastani Sungu \"Generative AI\" \"harm learning\" PNAS 2025 high school mathematics citation volume","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01Vz9uXiqkaMzQjogk9jtRow","content":[{"title":"Correction for Bastani et al., Generative AI without guardrails can harm learning: Evidence from high school mathematics | PNAS","url":"https://www.pnas.org/doi/10.1073/pnas.2518204122"},{"title":"Generative AI Without Guardrails Can Harm Learning: Evidence from High School Mathematics by Hamsa Bastani, Osbert Bastani, Alp Sungu, Haosen Ge, Özge Kabakcı, Rei Mariman :: SSRN","url":"https://papers.ssrn.com/sol3/papers.cfm?abstract_id=4895486"},{"title":"Generative AI without guardrails can harm learning: Evidence from high school mathematics - PubMed","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/40560616/"},{"title":"Correction for Bastani et al., Generative AI without guardrails can harm learning: Evidence from high school mathematics - PMC","url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12403119/"},{"title":"Generative AI without guardrails can harm learning: Evidence from high school mathematics | PNAS","url":"https://www.pnas.org/doi/10.1073/pnas.2422633122"},{"title":"Generative AI without guardrails can harm learning: Evidence from high school mathematics - Center for Health Incentives and Behavioral Economics (CHIBE)","url":"https://chibe.upenn.edu/publications/generative-ai-without-guardrails-can-harm-learning-evidence-from-high-school-mathematics/"},{"title":"Generative AI without guardrails can harm learning: Evidence from high school mathematics","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/393011815_Generative_AI_without_guardrails_can_harm_learning_Evidence_from_high_school_mathematics"},{"title":"The Effortless Trap: Productive Struggle, AI, and the Illusion of Learning","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2606.26181"},{"title":"A Meta-Analysis of LLM Effects on Students across Qualification, Socialisation, and Subjectification","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2509.22725"},{"title":"Transforming GenAI Policy to Prompting Instruction: An RCT of Scalable Prompting Interventions in a CS1 Course","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2602.16033"}]},"Based on the search results, I found the paper you're looking for:\n\nThe article \"Generative AI Without Guardrails Can Harm Learning: Evidence from High School Mathematics\" by Hamsa Bastani, Osbert Bastani, Alp Sungu, Haosen Ge, Özge Kabakcı, and Rei Mariman was published in the Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences (PNAS), volume 122, issue 26, in 2025.\n\nThe study involved a field experiment where nearly a thousand high school math students were provided with access to generative AI tutors. Two different generative AI tutors were deployed: one mimicking a standard ChatGPT interface (\"GPT Base\") and one with prompts designed to safeguard learning (\"GPT Tutor\").\n\n**Citation information:**\n- DOI: 10.1073/pnas.2422633122\n- Volume 122, Issue 26, published July 2025\n\nThe paper has been cited in several recent academic works and continues to be relevant to discussions about generative AI's impact on student learning."],"durationSeconds":28.011985083999985,"searchCount":1}}
